WEBVTT

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.980
In the year 1944,

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.150
a mysterious enemy, known as the Neuroi,

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.280
occupied the European Gallia region.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.740
But that very year,

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:20.040
the enemy was destroyed at the hands of the 501st Joint Fighter Wing,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.250
and Gallia was reclaimed.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:30.050
However, their battle is far from over.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.860
Neuroi spotted.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.700
It's identical to the humanoid one reported last year by the 501st.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.700
We see it, as well.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.780
Moving in to make contact.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.780
Roger that.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:11.420
<i>If this experimental mission to communicate with the Neuroi proves successful,</i>

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:15.260
<i>it just might bring about the end of the war.</i>

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.310
Wh-Why would the Neuroi
fire at one of their own?

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.060
What is that...

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.440
Suddenly, a large Neuroi hive
emerged in Venezian airspace.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.030
It obliterated the old hive,

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.990
and swallowed up all of northern Romagna in the blink of an eye.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:45.330
Humanity is once again drawn into the vicious war against the Neuroi.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.870
Takei, reporting in.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.540
Operation failed.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.300
I repeat...

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.050
Operation Trajanus has failed.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.850
Commence the attack!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.900
Take that!

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:31.910
<i>As we look with reverence to all that we owe you,</i>

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:38.040
<i>our beloved teachers...</i>

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:42.380
<i>Even within this garden of learning,</i>

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:45.010
Now, to give the graduation speech,

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:48.100
graduating class representative, Miyafuji Yoshika.
<i>my, how fast the years have passed.</i>

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.300
Thank you, sir!

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.390
<i>my, how fast the years have passed.</i>

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:58.060
Wow, this is so cool!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.770
It's a cherry blossom blizzard!

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.400
Look, Micchan!

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.280
Hey, Yoshika-chan...

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.030
Even though you graduated,
you're not going to high school?

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.540
Yeah, I come from a family of doctors.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.710
I can't wait to become a real one!

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.550
I guess we won't get to walk home together anymore.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.590
Hi, Michiko!

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.390
Oh, Grandpa!

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.930
Hi!

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:39.900
This spring, I'm actually going to the teacher's college in Yokohama.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.320
What? That's amazing!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.900
No, it isn't.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.450
Michiko always loved studying, even as a little girl.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.990
So you'll be a teacher when you grow up, huh?

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:54.490
You'll be a doctor at the clinic, too.

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.960
Oh, I guess I will. A doctor, huh?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.630
Ah, a warship!

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:02.210
Huh?

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.210
Wow! That's the Battleship Yamato.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:10.720
It's 263 meters long, capable of
generating 153,000 horsepower.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.800
It's the flagship of the allied fleet.

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:14.430
Wow!

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.390
It's huge!

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:21.610
The paper said it's leaving for a European tour.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:24.480
Europe...

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.940
So, it's bound for Europe...

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.540
Wh-What is it, Grandpa?

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.290
It's a bear.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.170
What's a bear doing so close to town?

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.550
Oh, no! It's hurt.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.420
Ah! Yoshika-chan!

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:50.470
H-Hey! That's dangerous, you two!

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:56.100
You'll be okay. I'll heal you right away.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.900
Good luck, Yoshika-chan.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.500
That's its mother!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.340
Run, Yoshika-chan!

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.800
Hold on... I'm almost done.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.680
Just a little more...

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:46.900
There you go. All better now.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.040
That girl is something else.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:03.960
Yoshika-chan!

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.090
Are you okay? Yoshika-chan!

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.550
Yoshika-chan?

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:16.180
That was so scary!

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.140
Geez...

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:31.780
<i>Dad... I graduated from middle school.</i>

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:38.530
<i>Now, just like I promised, I will use my power to help others,</i>

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.830
<i>right here, at this clinic.</i>

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.790
<i>Sakamoto-san...</i>

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:49.670
<i>Wow, it's already been six months
since the Battle of Britannia ended.</i>

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:03.350
<i>Everything started with this letter.</i>

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:05.690
Yoshika-chan! Yoshika-chan!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.650
What's the matter, Micchan?

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:12.320
No problem. I got it.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.040
Look! He's flying now, Micchan!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.080
Yeah! Thank you, Yoshika-chan!

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.250
Huh?

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.720
Was that a...

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.550
Ow...

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.220
...Witch?

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:50.360
Um, I am Suwa Amaki, with the 47th Flying Air Squadron.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:51.940
N-Nice to meet you.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:54.820
Is there a girl called Miyafuji Yoshika-san around here?

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.070
Y-Yes. That's me...

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.990
Oh, thank god!

00:09:58.990 --> 00:09:59.410
Huh?

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.200
This is a letter from Dr. Miyafuji.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.660
What? What?!

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.580
Mom! Grandma!

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:09.830
What is this?

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.960
Looks like some sort of drawing.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.840
I haven't the foggiest idea.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.710
Excuse me. Do you know what this is all about?

00:10:16.710 --> 00:10:20.800
I was just ordered to deliver this letter to you.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.600
I know about as much as you do.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.600
I'm sorry.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:27.810
I know!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:31.150
Sakamoto-san used to work with my dad, so I bet she'd know!

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.150
You mean Major Sakamoto, from the naval academy?

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.570
Yes! I'll go there tomorrow.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.940
I'll go with you!

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:03.930
It's done.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.670
It's been a long time since I last saw Sakamoto-san.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:41.090
But it's great they let you on the base, Yoshika-chan.

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:44.510
It's because they consider me one of the reserves.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:46.760
That's what Sakamoto-san said.

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.720
Oh... She's really scary, huh?

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:51.560
Not at all.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.140
She's really strict, but she has a kind heart.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:58.900
Actually, she told me not to come back here...

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.280
Huh? Why?

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:02.900
I don't know.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.700
Oh! Maybe that's the place.

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:07.120
Here?

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:10.490
Yeah. They said to wait here.

00:12:18.290 --> 00:12:21.460
This is Sakamoto-san's Striker Unit.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:28.470
When you fought with the Witches, did you wear one of those?

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:32.810
Yeah. It's nice to see one again.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:35.640
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.810
Hijikata-san!

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.020
Lovely to see you again.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:41.190
I must apologize.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:45.190
You came all the way here, but the Major is off base right now.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.780
Huh? Off base?

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:47.910
Where did she go?

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:50.200
I cannot answer that.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.540
She left her post, as a Witch training instructor, at the start of the year.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:57.040
I communicate with her from time to time.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:00.920
Um, I received a letter from my father yesterday.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.800
A letter from Dr. Miyafuji?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:08.220
But he passed away. So how...

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.340
I don't know.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:15.730
But I figured that Sakamoto-san might know, since she knew my father well.

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:17.520
Understood.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.730
I will give this letter to the Major when she returns.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.770
Oh! Please do. Thank you so much.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.480
Isn't that swell, Yoshika-chan?

00:13:25.480 --> 00:13:26.240
Yeah.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:27.780
Miyafuji-san!

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.070
Long time, no see!

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:33.160
The sweets you gave us were delicious!

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:35.490
We're ready for more, anytime!

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.410
You're so popular here, Yoshika-chan.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.250
Th-That's not true...

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:43.670
Officer Hijikata! You have an urgent communiqué from the Gallian military command!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:44.840
Gallia?

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:45.760
What is it?

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.670
Something strange is happening with the Neuroi in Europe.

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:49.930
What?

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:53.140
Neuroi?

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:56.470
From: Gallia-stationed Witches.

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:58.560
To: All allied commanding posts.

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:02.440
The Neuroi that emerged in
Venezian airspace yesterday

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.610
is considerably stronger than the previous ones.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.480
Venezia fell the same day.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:10.700
In response, the Romagna-based 504th Joint Allied Wing

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.660
engaged the enemy and
suffered massive casualties.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.330
They are no longer combat-capable.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.250
The Romagna-based 504th Joint Allied Wing is no longer combat-capable?

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.630
There are Fuso Witches in that squadron!

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:26.130
Don't you have a friend in Gallia, Yoshika-chan?

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.920
This is Hijikata, with the Fuso navy.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:31.430
Requesting sit-rep on the 504th in Romagna!

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:34.600
This is the Gallian military command post.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.810
Britannia Air Force Master Sergeant Lynette Bishop, responding.

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.060
Lynne-chan!

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.810
I don't know the details.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:45.110
We have requested reinforcements,

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:49.400
but we don't have enough Witches to mount a proper defense!

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:53.110
That's absurd. Even if we <i>are</i> low on Witches...

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:56.240
Also... we...

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:00.250
What's wrong? Do you copy, Sergeant Lynette?

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:01.330
It's impossible.

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:03.460
There is too much ionospheric interference. We can't...

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.380
Damn. So it's hopeless.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:08.000
I beg you! Please radio her again!

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:11.050
That girl is one of my best friends!

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:12.840
Radio her again!

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:14.220
I'll try.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.350
This is the Fuso Navy, Yokosuka base.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:17.760
Gallia military command, do you copy?!

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:19.270
This is the Fuso Navy. Do you copy?!

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.470
Lynne-chan...

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:23.730
Can you hear me, Lynne-chan? Say something, Lynne-chan!

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.320
Miyafuji, what are you doing here?

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.410
S-Sakamoto-san...

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.280
Sakamoto-san!

00:15:35.610 --> 00:15:37.660
It's Lynne-chan... She's in trouble!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.030
The Neuroi are back!

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.910
That has nothing to do with you!

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:43.790
It does! Lynne-chan is my friend!

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.710
Yoshika-chan...

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:51.050
Your friend, eh? You never change...

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:55.340
Just let us handle the situation in Europe.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:59.970
Miyafuji, you are not part of the Fuso military. You have no right to be here.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:02.180
Get the hell out!

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:05.020
Sakamoto-san...

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:22.950
The Fuso Navy is leaving immediately
on an emergency support mission in Europe.

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:23.950
Roger!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:28.630
<i>Another mysterious letter from Dr. Miyafuji...</i>

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:31.800
<i>Does it foreshadow a new battle?</i>

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:35.300
Hijikata, deliver this letter to the research lab.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:35.880
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.140
So this is the new Violet Lightning model?

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:44.770
Yes. Its magic engine output is higher than the previous Zero model.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.900
But... are you sure? You
haven't had a test flight yet.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.400
It's fine. Time's a luxury we don't have.

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.420
Wow! Look at the size of that flying boat!

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:18.050
<i>I see... That flying boat can make it to Europe in less than a week.</i>

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:22.640
That's...

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:25.680
A Striker Unit! A new version.

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:26.980
What is it, Yoshika-chan?

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:29.770
She's ready to fly again.

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:30.440
Huh?

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:34.530
Sakamoto-san is going to fight the Neuroi again,

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:37.400
even though she can't use shields anymore...

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.530
Ah! Yoshika-chan!

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:43.240
Major, in the last war, Miyafuji-san proved to be an ace in the hole.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:43.620
Why did you send her home?

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:47.120
Easy! Easy! Easy!

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.580
She's fought plenty already.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:55.500
She fulfilled her duty. That's all it is.

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:01.510
Striker launch unit, all loaded.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.550
Type-2 large flying boat
awaiting take-off command.

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:05.010
Take off!

00:18:14.980 --> 00:18:16.230
Sakamoto-san!

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:25.870
Miyafuji-san?!

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.250
H-Hold on!

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:41.090
Miyafuji Yoshika, taking off!

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.720
What?

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:48.470
You're not going anywhere, Miyafuji-san! No one ordered you to take off!

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:51.440
Please! I'm begging you! Let me go with Sakamoto-san!

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.770
B-But...

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:54.940
Yoshika-chan!

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:03.860
Micchan?

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:14.170
Micchan, I have to go.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.590
Have a safe flight. I'll be waiting for you.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:22.590
Okay. I'll be back.

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.600
Open the front hatch!

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:27.930
Roger that!

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:28.760
Aye-aye!

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:38.070
S-Such strong magic power...

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:39.360
Route set!

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.110
Wind velocity, check!

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:44.240
Striker Unit stabilizing bolt, released!

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:46.320
All clear for take off!

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:47.740
Take off!

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.380
What are those cherry blossoms doing there?

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:03.590
Don't tell me she...

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.600
Sakamoto-san!

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:12.020
What the heck do you think
you're doing?! Head back now!

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:15.560
Please, Sakamoto-san! Take me with you!

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:19.060
No! You have other things to do in Fuso!

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:22.320
But I... I...

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.490
...want to protect people!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.490
Protect?

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.580
Sakamoto-san?

00:20:36.250 --> 00:20:38.170
Get on board, Miyafuji!

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:40.380
Yes, ma'am!

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.650
I'm starving...

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.110
Want some canned food?

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:05.240
Liberion canned goods are nasty.

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:07.490
I wanna eat something tasty.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:10.280
You're talking crazy.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:12.660
We're practically out of supplies here.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:16.580
No! I wanna eat Yoshika's cooking! Yoshika's cooking!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:19.330
The more you yell, the hungrier you'll get.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:27.550
Yes, this is Yeager.

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:30.180
What? Seriously?

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.430
Understood. We're on our way.

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:35.680
Cheer up, Lucchini! A Fuso force is bringing supplies.

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:39.560
Woo-hoo! Food's a flyin' in!

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:42.310
We are currently above the Adriatic.

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:45.940
We'll soon arrive at the target, the Romagna military base.

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:46.480
Right.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:49.490
Ah... I'll finally get off this plane.

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:50.950
You've gotten soft, Miyafuji.

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:54.330
Whining about a flight as short as this one?

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.660
Sorry.

00:21:56.160 --> 00:22:00.670
Oh, yeah... Did you figure out
anything from my father's letter?

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:05.710
No. But I think it might concern Dr. Miyafuji's research.

00:22:05.710 --> 00:22:07.210
I handed it over to engineering.

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:11.180
It's probably a screw up at the
mail censors that's holding it up.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:12.050
Again?

00:22:13.970 --> 00:22:16.100
Unidentified craft detected on radar.

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:17.180
Approaching at high speed!

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:18.100
What?

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:24.230
What is it?!

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:26.610
An attack by an unidentified craft!

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:27.820
Engine 1 hit!

00:22:28.190 --> 00:22:30.570
Unidentified craft still incoming!

00:22:33.570 --> 00:22:34.620
It couldn't be...

00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:37.950
Neuroi...

00:24:12.550 --> 00:24:16.050
This young girl has once again cast her body into the flames of war.

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:18.010
However, she is not alone.

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:20.600
She has many friends in whom she can trust.

00:24:20.600 --> 00:24:24.850
Next time on <i>Strike Witches 2:</i>
The Legendary Witches
